verses.text:
For scripture contains this:
“See, I set down in Zion a stone,
a cornerstone, chosen, of great worth;
whoever puts his trust in him will never be disgraced.”{c}

To you who trust, then, there is honor; but for those who do not trust,
“the stone which the builders rejected
has become the head of the corner,”{d}

For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous,
and his ears are open to their prayer;
but the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.”{b}

And
“if it is hard for the righteous to be saved,
where will the godless and the sinner appear?”{f}

Likewise, you younger ones, be subject to those who are older. All of you, tie on humility like an apron in dealing with each other, for
“God sets himself against the arrogant,
but to the lowly he gives grace.”{b}
